{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBTryVJ2i8PQ1ZA2Miif","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 7 (Fe 0.69, Sb 0.31) as the best composition. It had the highest EQE of the three I measured, at 0.0164%. The merit budget was only three measurements, so this is the best of three samples along the line, not a confirmed library optimum.\n\n| Index | Composition (Fe:Sb) | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 7 | 0.69 : 0.31 | **0.0164** |\n| 20 | 0.31 : 0.69 | 0.0053 |\n| 14 | 0.48 : 0.52 (about 1:1) | 0.0035 |\n\n- **How I chose the samples:** I measured near the 1:1 composition first, where FeSbO4 is a known photoanode. Then I measured one point on the iron-rich side and one on the antimony-rich side.\n- **XRD:** I used 3 of the 5 XRD scans (indices 5, 14 and 22). All three are dominated by the same set of peaks, so the whole range seems to be mostly one phase. Only the antimony-rich sample (index 22) showed small extra peaks. I identified that phase as rutile-type FeSbO4 from background knowledge, not a checked peak match. Since the phase barely changes, XRD didn't help pick where to measure.\n- **Where the true best may be:** index 7 is about 3–5 times better than the other two points, which suggests the peak is somewhere on the iron-rich side. I never measured indices 0–6 (Fe 0.74–0.84), so a composition there could beat index 7."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":8440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"output_tokens":514,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13b506f0-979a-493b-a75c-139cdd4004bf","uuid":"c5b86161-255f-4869-aec7-6b604212d293","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:33:43.474Z","request